1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,660
I'd been driving for
almost 11 hours when the

2
00:00:02,660 --> 00:00:04,500
detour signs pushed me off the interstate.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:08,000
The road narrowed to two
lanes, then the radio

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,360
lost its station, and for a long time the

5
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:12,140
only light out there
was my own headlights.

6
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:16,860
Around two in the morning, I saw a gas
station sign glowing over the fields.

7
00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:22,060
The pumps were on, the store was dark, and
there was one other car parked by the air

8
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:24,860
machine with its engine
running and nobody inside.

9
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:28,160
This was in October, about six years ago.

10
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:33,040
I was 24 and moving back home to Missouri
after a job in Colorado fell apart.

11
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,380
Everything I owned was in the backseat
of a Corolla with a cracked windshield.

12
00:00:37,940 --> 00:00:40,200
I'd planned to stop for the
night in a motel somewhere

13
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:42,700
in western Kansas, but I kept telling

14
00:00:42,740 --> 00:00:45,820
myself one more hour, and
by the time the detour

15
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:47,720
came up, I was too tired to be smart

16
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:48,520
about it.

17
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:51,680
The last real town I
passed was a place with

18
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:54,240
one stoplight and a grain elevator lit up

19
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:55,040
like a ship.

20
00:00:55,520 --> 00:00:57,780
After that, the map on
my phone turned into a

21
00:00:57,780 --> 00:01:00,340
gray blank with a single blue line through

22
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:01,160
it.

23
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:03,360
When the detour started,
there was a pickup truck

24
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:05,420
ahead of me for a while, the only other

25
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:06,380
headlights for miles.

26
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:10,380
At a crossroads with no
signs at all, it turned

27
00:01:10,380 --> 00:01:12,540
onto a dirt road, and its lights went out

28
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:15,600
almost immediately, like it had
pulled over and shut off the engine.

29
00:01:16,140 --> 00:01:18,720
I remember thinking that
was a strange place to stop.

30
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:22,140
I kept going straight, because
the orange arrows told me to.

31
00:01:22,860 --> 00:01:25,340
I pulled up to the pump,
farthest from the other car.

32
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:29,980
It was an older station wagon, dark green
with wood panels on the sides and a bumper

33
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:32,120
sticker that said, Proud
Parent of an Honor Student,

34
00:01:32,260 --> 00:01:33,500
with the name of the school scratched

35
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:34,300
off.

36
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:36,300
The exhaust was rising in the cold.

37
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:38,680
The headlights were off,
but the dome light was

38
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:40,840
on, and I could see a
jacket on the passenger

39
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:42,760
seat and a fast food bag on the dashboard.

40
00:01:43,660 --> 00:01:45,780
I figured whoever it
belonged to was in the

41
00:01:45,780 --> 00:01:46,700
bathroom around the side of the building.

42
00:01:47,820 --> 00:01:49,280
Then I noticed the backseat.

43
00:01:49,940 --> 00:01:52,500
There was a child's booster
seat behind the driver,

44
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:55,120
and a stuffed rabbit sitting in it,

45
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:57,180
turned around so it faced the rear window.

46
00:01:57,840 --> 00:02:03,000
A pair of small sneakers sat on the floor
mat underneath, neatly side by side, like

47
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,760
someone had taken them off and
planned to put them right back on.

48
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:08,860
Whoever had been driving
that car hadn't been alone.

49
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:11,100
I filled the tank and waited.

50
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:12,440
I don't know why I waited.

51
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:16,760
I think I wanted to see someone walk back
to that car, just so I could stop thinking

52
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:17,560
about it.

53
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:18,900
Nobody came.

54
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:21,540
The pump clicked off,
the screen asked if I

55
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:23,840
wanted a receipt, and the whole time that

56
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:27,440
engine kept idling, steady, like
it had been running for hours.

57
00:02:28,420 --> 00:02:29,800
I didn't go check the bathroom.

58
00:02:30,140 --> 00:02:31,720
I got back in my car and left.

59
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:35,860
As I pulled away, I looked in the
rearview mirror one last time.

60
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:38,400
The dome light in the wagon was still on.

61
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:42,060
The stuffed rabbit in the
backseat was facing forward now.

62
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:46,640
About twenty minutes later, the
detour signs ended at a truck stop.

63
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:49,900
It was the first real building
I'd seen in a long time.

64
00:02:50,660 --> 00:02:53,040
A diner on one side, a
couple of semis parked

65
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:55,240
out back with their running lights on, and

66
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:58,980
a sign that said, Open 24 hours,
with two of the letters burned out.

67
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:01,940
I parked near the
entrance because I needed

68
00:03:01,940 --> 00:03:04,180
coffee, and I needed to sit somewhere with

69
00:03:04,180 --> 00:03:05,000
people for a while.

70
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:09,880
Inside, it was warm and smelled
like burnt coffee and bacon grease.

71
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:12,300
There was a trucker at
the counter, reading

72
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:14,720
his phone, an older man asleep in a booth

73
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:16,160
by the window, and one waitress.

74
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:21,880
Her name tag said D. She looked about fifty,
and she called me honey before I'd even

75
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:22,680
sat down.

76
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:25,960
I took a booth facing
the door, ordered coffee

77
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,960
and a slice of pie, and started looking at

78
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:32,280
the map on my phone, trying to figure
out how far I was from anything.

79
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:35,720
That's when the couple came in.

80
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:38,260
They were young, maybe my age.

81
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:41,400
The guy wore a gray
hoodie, and the girl had

82
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:43,440
on a denim jacket that
was too thin for the

83
00:03:43,440 --> 00:03:44,240
weather.

84
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:46,420
It had started to rain
outside, and the shoulders

85
00:03:46,420 --> 00:03:47,920
of their jackets were dark with it.

86
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:51,840
They were arguing in that low,
tight way people argue in public.

87
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:55,900
As they walked past my booth, the
girl said, Every single time, Ray.

88
00:03:56,060 --> 00:03:57,240
Every single time.

89
00:03:58,040 --> 00:03:58,840
He didn't answer.

90
00:03:59,460 --> 00:04:01,860
They sat two booths down
from me, across the

91
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:04,280
aisle, and D. went over with menus and two

92
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:05,340
waters like it was nothing.

93
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:07,900
I didn't think much about it.

94
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:09,320
I ate my pie.

95
00:04:09,900 --> 00:04:12,180
I heard bits of their
conversation, something about

96
00:04:12,180 --> 00:04:14,540
a wrong turn and whose idea it had been

97
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:15,420
to leave so late.

98
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:18,640
The girl had a laugh that
wasn't really a laugh.

99
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:21,140
At one point, Ray said, We'll be fine.

100
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:22,400
We're almost there.

101
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:24,140
She didn't say anything back.

102
00:04:25,340 --> 00:04:27,820
D. came by to refill my coffee
and asked where I was headed.

103
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:31,520
When I told her Missouri, she nodded
like she'd heard it a thousand times.

104
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:34,420
Then she glanced at the window
and lowered her voice a little.

105
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:38,760
She said, When you leave, honey, follow
the signs back to the interstate.

106
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:42,140
Don't take the old county road, even
if your phone tells you it's shorter.

107
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:43,680
I asked her why.

108
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:46,680
She just smiled, said
the road wasn't kept up

109
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:48,480
anymore, and went back behind the counter.

110
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:51,400
After a while, I got up
to use the restroom.

111
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:53,980
It was at the end of a short
hallway past the kitchen.

112
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:56,280
I remember the hallway
because one of the fluorescent

113
00:04:56,280 --> 00:04:57,760
lights was flickering, and there

114
00:04:57,760 --> 00:05:01,100
was a corkboard on the wall with business
cards and a flyer for a missing dog.

115
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:03,840
I was in there maybe
three or four minutes.

116
00:05:04,060 --> 00:05:06,640
I washed my hands,
splashed water on my face,

117
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:08,840
and looked at myself in
the mirror, thinking

118
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:10,440
I really needed to find a bed.

119
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:15,660
When I came out and walked back toward my
booth, the bell over the front door rang.

120
00:05:16,380 --> 00:05:17,420
It was them.

121
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:18,500
The same couple.

122
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:23,400
Gray hoodie, thin denim jacket, the
shoulders of both jackets dark with rain.

123
00:05:24,140 --> 00:05:26,420
They walked in the same
way, him a step ahead,

124
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:28,460
her a little behind with her arms crossed.

125
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:30,700
And as they passed me, the girl said,

126
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:32,740
Every single time, Ray.

127
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:34,260
Every single time.

128
00:05:35,020 --> 00:05:36,240
I stopped in the aisle.

129
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:39,500
I looked over at the booth two down
from mine, where they'd been sitting.

130
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:41,080
It was empty.

131
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:44,540
No menus, no glasses, no
wet rings on the table.

132
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:47,420
It had been wiped down like
nobody had used it all night.

133
00:05:48,180 --> 00:05:49,860
They sat in that same booth.

134
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:54,660
Dee came over with two menus and two waters,
and she smiled at them, and she said,

135
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:56,100
Evening, you two.

136
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:57,260
Rough night out there?

137
00:05:57,840 --> 00:06:00,080
Exactly how you'd greet
someone who just walked in.

138
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:02,840
I stood there long enough
that I felt stupid,

139
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:05,000
so I made myself walk past their booth on

140
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:05,820
the way back to mine.

141
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:08,400
Up close, I could see the girl's jacket.

142
00:06:08,980 --> 00:06:11,060
The rain had soaked into
the denim in exactly the

143
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:13,520
same shape as before, a dark patch across

144
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:15,800
both shoulders and a long
streak down one arm.

145
00:06:17,060 --> 00:06:19,280
Ray had his wrist on the table,
and his watch caught the light.

146
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,500
It was one of those old digital watches.

147
00:06:21,860 --> 00:06:25,660
It read 214, and while I
watched, it didn't change.

148
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:29,580
I sat down because I didn't
know what else to do.

149
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:31,240
My coffee was still there.

150
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:32,300
My plate was still there.

151
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:33,760
I watched them.

152
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:36,540
I kept waiting for one
of them to look at me,

153
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:38,780
or laugh, or for this to turn into some

154
00:06:38,780 --> 00:06:39,580
kind of joke.

155
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:41,500
Ray was rubbing his eyes.

156
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:44,200
The girl was looking out the
window at the parking lot.

157
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:47,000
They were having the same conversation.

158
00:06:47,780 --> 00:06:48,580
Wrong turn.

159
00:06:48,760 --> 00:06:49,560
Leaving too late.

160
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:51,600
And then Ray said, We'll be fine.

161
00:06:51,820 --> 00:06:52,620
We're almost there.

162
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:54,820
I looked at the trucker at the counter.

163
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:57,460
He hadn't looked up from
his phone the whole time.

164
00:06:57,860 --> 00:07:00,240
The old man in the window
booth was still asleep.

165
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:03,680
Nobody else in that room seemed
to think anything was wrong.

166
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:07,780
I don't know where the nerve came
from, but I walked over to their booth.

167
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:10,820
I stood at the end of
the table and asked, as

168
00:07:10,820 --> 00:07:13,100
normally as I could, if they'd just gotten

169
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:13,900
there.

170
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:15,140
The girl didn't look at me.

171
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:16,940
She kept staring at the parking lot.

172
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:21,060
Ray looked up, and for a second, I thought
he was going to say something real.

173
00:07:21,540 --> 00:07:24,480
His eyes were red, like he hadn't
slept in a very long time.

174
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:28,260
Then he said, very calmly, We'll be fine.

175
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:29,640
We're almost there.

176
00:07:30,060 --> 00:07:32,780
He said it to me, exactly
the way he'd said it to her.

177
00:07:33,540 --> 00:07:35,820
I left a twenty on the
table and walked out.

178
00:07:36,180 --> 00:07:37,080
I didn't wait for change.

179
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:40,920
When I got outside, the rain had
stopped, and the parking lot was dry.

180
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:42,120
Completely dry.

181
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:43,460
No puddles.

182
00:07:43,700 --> 00:07:44,740
Nothing wet on my windshield.

183
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:48,080
I stood there for a second,
looking at the ground.

184
00:07:48,780 --> 00:07:51,020
Then I got in my car,
locked the doors, and sat

185
00:07:51,020 --> 00:07:52,780
with the engine running for a long time.

186
00:07:54,320 --> 00:07:56,620
I didn't want to drive past
that gas station again.

187
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:58,880
I didn't want to go back inside, either.

188
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:01,880
So I just sat there
until the sky started to

189
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:03,880
turn gray, and then I followed the signs

190
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:04,680
back to the interstate.

191
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:08,020
I didn't pass the gas
station on the way back.

192
00:08:08,620 --> 00:08:10,600
I took the same road, I'm sure of that.

193
00:08:10,880 --> 00:08:12,100
It just wasn't there.

194
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,980
I had a dash cam back then,
one of those cheap ones

195
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:17,820
that records over itself every few hours.

196
00:08:18,720 --> 00:08:21,180
When I finally got home
and checked it, most

197
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:22,500
of that night had
already been overwritten.

198
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:26,060
The only file left starts
as I pull into the truck

199
00:08:26,060 --> 00:08:27,900
stop parking lot at 2.14 in the morning.

200
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:31,620
I park, the camera keeps
recording, and about

201
00:08:31,620 --> 00:08:33,840
a minute later, the dark
green station wagon

202
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:35,800
pulls into the spot right in front of me.

203
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:39,120
Engine running, dome
light on, nobody inside.

204
00:08:40,160 --> 00:08:42,840
The date on that clip is October 14th.

205
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:45,720
The year is the one before
I ever drove that road.

206
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:49,240
I still drive that interstate
a couple of times a year.

207
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,280
If the detour signs are
up, I don't take them.

208
00:08:52,900 --> 00:08:55,320
I find the last town
before the exit, I park

209
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:57,580
somewhere well lit, and I sleep in my car

210
00:08:57,580 --> 00:08:58,380
until morning.

